    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.session\n\n### Description\n\nMini.session didn't work correctly on windows at first, at startup it just kept saying `(mini.sessions) \"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\B4mbus\\\\\\\\AppData\\\\\\\\Local\\\\\\\\nvim-data\\\\\\\\session\" is not a directory path.` So I changed it manually to `vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '\\\\sessions\\\\` and it doesn't display that error anymore, but the paths that are displayed use `%` or `++` as a separator instead of `\\`.\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.0-dev-922-g42e9fe7d9\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\nContents of `minimal.lua`:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.sessions').setup({\r\n  directory = require('plenary.path')\r\n    :new(vim.fn.stdpath('data'))\r\n    :joinpath('sessions\\\\')\r\n    .filename\r\n})\r\n\r\n```\r\n3. Same thing\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nPaths displayed properly, that is either `F:\\prv.vim` or `f/prv.vim`.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nPaths are displayed incorrectly, with `++` and `%`.\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/75364377/192162911-ce51a96d-c728-4a5c-80d9-e3941c123327.png)\r\n\r\n(here with minimal config)\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/75364377/192163038-97e44cfe-f4b5-4c1b-9fd1-93aa4f962dec.png)\r\n",
