            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "If you are willing to spend your time here, sure, go for it!\r\n\r\nOn first and second glances it is hard to see why this might be separate issues, though. In 'mini.starter' session names are taken directly from `MiniSessions.detected` (see [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/17f40dc27a46dbca97af3a29688c5ea6ab444423/lua/mini/starter.lua#L461-L468)). And `MiniSessions.detected` is computed during `require('mini.sessions').setup()`.\r\n\r\nFor reference:\r\n- [Here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/17f40dc27a46dbca97af3a29688c5ea6ab444423/lua/mini/sessions.lua#L449-L467) is how global sessions are detected.\r\n- [Here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/17f40dc27a46dbca97af3a29688c5ea6ab444423/lua/mini/sessions.lua#L102) and [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/17f40dc27a46dbca97af3a29688c5ea6ab444423/lua/mini/sessions.lua#L53) is how default directory for global sessions is computed. My first guess is that problem is somewhere here.",
