            "body": "@B4mbus, can you look into this again please? Is this issue still there?\r\n\r\nThe 'mini.sessions' module now automatically creates missing directory for global sessions, so there shouldn't be any errors (see #134). The issue of weird 'mini.starter' behavior may still persist.\r\n\r\nI have a follow up question. What files are **actually there** in directory `vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '\\\\sessions\\\\` (to which you changed). Because I suspect that those can be actual base names of files there, which were created earlier by some other sessions management tool.",
